{
  "level_code": 2,
  "lessons": [
    {
      "slug": "past-was-were",
      "title": "Past of to be: was and were",
      "summary": "Talk about where people were and how things were.",
      "estimated_minutes": 10,
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "learn",
          "title": "was / were",
          "body_md": "| | past of *to be* |\n|---|---|\n| I / he / she / it | **was** |\n| you / we / they | **were** |\n\n**Negative:** *wasn't* (was not), *weren't* (were not).\n\n**Question:** ***Was** it cold? **Were** they at home?*"
        },
        {
          "kind": "see",
          "title": "Examples",
          "body_md": "- *I **was** at the doctor's yesterday.*\n- *The film **was** really funny.*\n- *We **weren't** at school last Friday.*\n- ***Were** you tired after the trip?* — *Yes, I **was**.*"
        },
        {
          "kind": "try",
          "title": "Try it",
          "body_md": "Try it.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "was-try-1",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "My grandparents ___ farmers.",
              "options": [
                "was",
                "were",
                "are been"
              ],
              "answer": "were",
              "hint": "they → ?",
              "explanation": "*My grandparents* = *they*, so *were*."
            },
            {
              "id": "was-try-2",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "___ the shop open yesterday?",
              "options": [
                "Was",
                "Were",
                "Did"
              ],
              "answer": "Was",
              "explanation": "*The shop* = *it*, so the question starts with *Was*."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "check",
          "title": "Check",
          "body_md": "Answer the questions.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "was-check-1",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "It ___ very hot last summer.",
              "options": [
                "was",
                "were",
                "is"
              ],
              "answer": "was",
              "explanation": "*It* + past = *was*."
            },
            {
              "id": "was-check-2",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "You ___ late this morning.",
              "options": [
                "was",
                "were",
                "be"
              ],
              "answer": "were",
              "explanation": "*You* always goes with *were*."
            },
            {
              "id": "was-check-3",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "Which is the negative?",
              "options": [
                "They weren't happy.",
                "They were happy.",
                "Were they happy?"
              ],
              "answer": "They weren't happy.",
              "explanation": "*weren't* = *were not*."
            },
            {
              "id": "was-check-4",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "\"Was Sam at the party?\" \"No, he ___.\"",
              "options": [
                "wasn't",
                "weren't",
                "didn't"
              ],
              "answer": "wasn't",
              "explanation": "Short answer with *he*: *No, he wasn't.*"
            },
            {
              "id": "was-check-5",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "Where ___ you last night?",
              "options": [
                "was",
                "were",
                "did"
              ],
              "answer": "were",
              "explanation": "*you* → *were*: *Where were you?*"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "past-simple-regular",
      "title": "Past simple: regular verbs",
      "summary": "Add -ed to talk about finished actions.",
      "estimated_minutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "learn",
          "title": "Finished actions",
          "body_md": "We use the **past simple** for actions that finished in the past.\n\nRegular verbs add **-ed**, the same for everyone: *I work**ed**, she work**ed**, they work**ed**.*\n\nSpelling:\n- *live → live**d*** (ends in *e*: add *d*)\n- *study → stud**ied*** (consonant + *y*: *y → ied*)\n- *stop → stop**ped*** (short verb, one vowel + one consonant: double it)\n- *play → play**ed*** (vowel + *y*: just add *ed*)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "see",
          "title": "Examples",
          "body_md": "*Last weekend I **visited** my aunt. We **cooked** lunch and **watched** a film. On Sunday it **rained**, so I **stayed** at home and **studied**.*"
        },
        {
          "kind": "try",
          "title": "Try it",
          "body_md": "Try it.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "reg-try-1",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "Yesterday I ___ my room.",
              "options": [
                "clean",
                "cleaned",
                "cleaning"
              ],
              "answer": "cleaned",
              "hint": "Add -ed.",
              "explanation": "Past simple: *clean + ed = cleaned*."
            },
            {
              "id": "reg-try-2",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "What is the past of \"try\"?",
              "options": [
                "tryed",
                "tried",
                "trys"
              ],
              "answer": "tried",
              "explanation": "Consonant + *y* → *ied*: *tried*."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "check",
          "title": "Check",
          "body_md": "Answer the questions.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "reg-check-1",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "She ___ in Rome for two years.",
              "options": [
                "live",
                "lived",
                "liveed"
              ],
              "answer": "lived",
              "explanation": "*live* ends in *e*, so add *d*: *lived*."
            },
            {
              "id": "reg-check-2",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "The bus ___ suddenly.",
              "options": [
                "stoped",
                "stopped",
                "stopt"
              ],
              "answer": "stopped",
              "explanation": "*stop* doubles the *p*: *stopped*."
            },
            {
              "id": "reg-check-3",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "We ___ football after school.",
              "options": [
                "played",
                "plaied",
                "plays"
              ],
              "answer": "played",
              "explanation": "Vowel + *y*: just add *ed*: *played*."
            },
            {
              "id": "reg-check-4",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "Which sentence is in the past?",
              "options": [
                "I walk to work.",
                "I walked to work.",
                "I am walking to work."
              ],
              "answer": "I walked to work.",
              "explanation": "*walked* is past simple."
            },
            {
              "id": "reg-check-5",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "He ___ for the exam all night.",
              "options": [
                "studyed",
                "studied",
                "studies"
              ],
              "answer": "studied",
              "explanation": "*study* → *studied*."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "past-simple-irregular",
      "title": "Past simple: irregular verbs",
      "summary": "Learn common verbs that do not use -ed.",
      "estimated_minutes": 14,
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "learn",
          "title": "Irregular verbs",
          "body_md": "Many common verbs have a special past form. Learn them by heart.\n\n| verb | past | verb | past |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| go | **went** | have | **had** |\n| see | **saw** | eat | **ate** |\n| come | **came** | make | **made** |\n| take | **took** | buy | **bought** |\n| get | **got** | write | **wrote** |\n| say | **said** | think | **thought** |"
        },
        {
          "kind": "see",
          "title": "A story",
          "body_md": "*On Saturday I **went** to the market. I **saw** my friend Leo there. We **bought** some fruit and **had** coffee. Then we **took** the bus home. Leo **said** it **was** a great day.*"
        },
        {
          "kind": "try",
          "title": "Try it",
          "body_md": "Try it.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "irr-try-1",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "Last year we ___ to Spain.",
              "options": [
                "goed",
                "went",
                "gone"
              ],
              "answer": "went",
              "hint": "It is irregular.",
              "explanation": "The past of *go* is *went*."
            },
            {
              "id": "irr-try-2",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "I ___ a letter to my grandmother.",
              "options": [
                "writed",
                "wrote",
                "write"
              ],
              "answer": "wrote",
              "explanation": "The past of *write* is *wrote*."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "check",
          "title": "Check",
          "body_md": "Answer the questions.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "irr-check-1",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "She ___ a new phone last week.",
              "options": [
                "buyed",
                "bought",
                "buys"
              ],
              "answer": "bought",
              "explanation": "The past of *buy* is *bought*."
            },
            {
              "id": "irr-check-2",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "We ___ pizza for dinner.",
              "options": [
                "ate",
                "eated",
                "eat"
              ],
              "answer": "ate",
              "explanation": "The past of *eat* is *ate*."
            },
            {
              "id": "irr-check-3",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "They ___ home very late.",
              "options": [
                "comed",
                "came",
                "come"
              ],
              "answer": "came",
              "explanation": "The past of *come* is *came*."
            },
            {
              "id": "irr-check-4",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "I ___ a strange noise in the night.",
              "options": [
                "heard",
                "heared",
                "hear"
              ],
              "answer": "heard",
              "explanation": "The past of *hear* is *heard*."
            },
            {
              "id": "irr-check-5",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "He ___ that he was busy.",
              "options": [
                "sayed",
                "said",
                "says"
              ],
              "answer": "said",
              "explanation": "The past of *say* is *said*."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "past-simple-questions-negatives",
      "title": "Past simple: questions and negatives",
      "summary": "Use did and didn't to ask and say no about the past.",
      "estimated_minutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "learn",
          "title": "did / didn't",
          "body_md": "- **Negative:** *didn't* + base verb: *I **didn't go** to work.* (not *didn't went*)\n- **Question:** *Did* + subject + base verb: ***Did** you **see** the match?*\n- **Short answers:** *Yes, I did. / No, I didn't.*\n- **Wh- questions:** *Where **did** you **go**? What **did** she **buy**?*\n\nWith *was/were* we do **not** use *did*: *Were you tired?* (not *Did you be tired?*)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "see",
          "title": "Examples",
          "body_md": "- ***Did** you **enjoy** the concert?* — *Yes, I **did**.*\n- *She **didn't like** the food.*\n- *What time **did** the train **leave**?*\n- *We **didn't have** time for lunch.*"
        },
        {
          "kind": "try",
          "title": "Try it",
          "body_md": "Try it.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "dq-try-1",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "I ___ my homework yesterday.",
              "options": [
                "didn't finish",
                "didn't finished",
                "not finished"
              ],
              "answer": "didn't finish",
              "hint": "didn't + base verb",
              "explanation": "After *didn't*, use the base verb: *didn't finish*."
            },
            {
              "id": "dq-try-2",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "___ you call your mother?",
              "options": [
                "Did",
                "Do",
                "Were"
              ],
              "answer": "Did",
              "explanation": "Past simple questions start with *Did*."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "check",
          "title": "Check",
          "body_md": "Answer the questions.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "dq-check-1",
              "type": "single_choice",
              "prompt": "Where ___ you go on holiday?",
