      "sections": [
        {
          "kind": "learn",
          "title": "be going to + verb",
          "body_md": "Use **be going to** for plans you have already made, and for things we can see are going to happen.\n\n*I**'m going to** visit my cousin. She**'s going to** study law. They**'re going to** move house.*\n\n**Negative:** *I'm not going to ...*  **Question:** ***Are** you **going to** ...?*\n\nLook at those clouds! It**'s going to** rain. (we can see it)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "see",
          "title": "Plans for the summer",
          "body_md": "*This summer **I'm going to** learn to drive. My sister **is going to** work in a hotel. We **aren't going to** travel abroad, but we **are going to** visit the coast for a weekend.*"
        },
        {
